# context-kit scratch output
# Note: ignore *contents* (`.context-kit/*`) rather than the directory
# (`.context-kit/`). Git cannot re-include a file with `!path` if its
# parent directory is ignored, so the directory-form would silently
# defeat the verify.yaml allowlist below.
.context-kit/*
# BUT: track verify.yaml — it's the canonical-docs config that drives
# `context-kit verify`, not scratch. Without it CI's verifier falls
# through to active-docs scoring and misclassifies legitimate
# DOC_ONLY findings as CONFLICT (see PR #2059 investigation).
!.context-kit/verify.yaml
connections-report.json
context-coverage.json
context-doctor.json
context-hotpath.txt
context-inspect-core.json
context-inspect.json

